# Consensus runtime configuration (phase0 through Gloas)

Generated by `scripts/consensus-preset-generate.py`. Do not edit by hand; regenerate, and
check with `python3 -I scripts/consensus-preset-generate.py --check`.

Source: `ethereum/consensus-specs` `v1.7.0-beta.4` (commit `aa16bb4c156184e9548a997d53efaf2a228a6304`), files and SHA-256:

* `configs/minimal.yaml` `bf60d06fca6ea9fbcc97a63f54a9b5f1a2161d734514c07e7087c170f671ea44`
* `configs/mainnet.yaml` `30a37b4e8a53c3e9296a5b64224d8a3ca8785f7ce5f5cba157d2fc19dd6ee902`

A configuration holds the run-time variables of the specification (`configs/README.md`).
`Config` has one field per variable of `configs/<name>.yaml` that a phase0 to Gloas
specification file mentions, spelled as in the specification. Left out, because no
phase0 to Gloas specification file mentions them:

`CONFIG_NAME`, `HEZE_FORK_VERSION`, `HEZE_FORK_EPOCH`, `EIP8321_FORK_VERSION`, `EIP8321_FORK_EPOCH`, `EIP8198_FORK_VERSION`, `EIP8198_FORK_EPOCH`, `INCLUSION_LIST_DUE_BPS`, `SLOT_DURATION_MS_EIP8198`, `MAX_REQUEST_INCLUSION_LIST`, `MIN_SLOTS_FOR_INCLUSION_LISTS_REQUESTS`, `MAX_TRANSACTIONS_BYTES_PER_INCLUSION_LIST`, `MIN_BLOB_DATA_RETENTION_MS`.

Types follow the value form: decimal `Nat`; four bytes `Bytes`; an execution address
`Adr`; a 32-byte hash `B256`; `BLOB_SCHEDULE` a list of `BlobScheduleEntry` and
`GAS_LIMIT_SCHEDULE` a list of `GasLimitScheduleEntry`.
-/


